          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong suplattice
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            that has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/joins"} joins
            of arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            (and in particular is a join-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"}> semilattice
            ). By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            for posets, a suplattice necessarily has all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meets
            as well and so is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattice"} complete lattice
            %strong suplattice homomorphism
            preserves joins, but not necessarily meets. Furthermore, a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} large
            semilattice which has all
            %em small
            joins need not have all meets, but might still be considered a large suplattice (even though it may not even be a lattice).
          %p
            Dually, an
            %strong inflattice
            is a poset which has all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meets"} meets
            %strong inflattice homomorphism
            is a monotone function that preserves all meets.
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            (dual to a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SupLat"} SupLat
            of suplattices and suplattice homomorphisms admits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            which represents “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+maps"}> bilinear maps
            ”, i.e. functions which preserve joins separately in each variable. Under this tensor product, the category of suplattices is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-autonomous+category"} star-autonomous category
            in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizing+object"} dualizing object
            is the suplattice dual to the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth-values"} truth-values
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup+object"} semigroup
            in this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantale"} quantale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frames"} frames
            as a special case when the quantale is idempotent and unital. Modules over them are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules+over+quantales"} modules over quantales
            (quantic modules with special case of localic modules, used in the localic analogue of the Grothendieck’s descent theory in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#JoyalTierney84"} Joyal-Tierney 84
          %h2#the_free_suplattice_on_a_poset The free suplattice on a poset
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi SupLat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Poset
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U \colon SupLat \to Poset
          %p
            This has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Poset
                  %mo →
                  %mi SupLat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \colon Poset \to SupLat
          %p
            where for any poset
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(P)
            is the poset of downsets of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/downset"} downset
            of a poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subseteq P
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S, s' \le s \quad  \implies \quad s' \in S.
          %p
            This set of all downsets in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{P}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{P}
            that sends each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in P
            to its
            %strong principal
            downset
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi s
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{s \in P : \; s \le p \}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antichain"} antichain
          %p
            To understand this description of the free suplattice on a poset, some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            is useful.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} Preorders
            are the same as
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Bool
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            with two objects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            and one nontrivial morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \implies T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            correspond in a one-to-one way with
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon P^{op} \to Bool
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon C^{op} \to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \colon P \to \hat{P}
            that sends each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in P
            to its principal downset is the
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            on a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocomplete category
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{P}
            is the free cocomplete
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
          %h2#the_category_of_suplattices The category of suplattices
          %p
            The category of suplattices is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+adjunction"} monadic
            over the category of posets, and each algebra structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi: \hat{P} \to P
            is left adjoint to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y: P \to \hat{P}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+categories"} total categories
            in the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Bool
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bool
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched
            sense. Notice that algebra structure maps, being left adjoints, are cocontinuous and therefore suplattice morphisms. This makes the monad a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monad"} commutative monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SupLat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SupLat
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+closed+category"} symmetric monoidal closed category
            where the internal hom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(P, Q)
            between two suplattices is the suplattice of cocontinuous maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Q
            according to the poset version of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SupLat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SupLat
            is also monadic over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P: Set \to Set
            is the covariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            functor. It therefore is a complete and cocomplete
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr-exact+category"} Barr-exact category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            of this monad is equivalent to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rel"} Rel
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rel
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel
            may be thought of as the free suplattices.
          %p
            As stated above, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+closed+category"} symmetric monoidal closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SupLat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SupLat
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-autonomous+category"} star-autonomous category
            where the star-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            takes a suplattice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            poset
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^{op}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inflattice"} inflattice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            (where we use an internal covariant power-object functor to form an appropriate monad). Thus the tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \otimes Q
            may be formed as the suplattice
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(P, Q^{op})^{op}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi SupLat
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi SupLat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast = (-)^{op}: SupLat^{op} \to SupLat
          %p
            (which takes a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: P \to Q
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mi op
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Q
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^{op}: Q^{op} \to P^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is right adjoint to
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#JoyalTierney84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miles+Tierney"} Miles Tierney
